<title>ECUADOR: Quito stock trading suspended over bomb threat.</title>
<headline>Quito stock trading suspended over bomb threat.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading was suspended on the Quito stock exchange Thursday because of a bomb threat at a bank building which houses the bourse, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The receptionist told us there were police orders to empty the building because of a bomb threat, supposedly in (the local branch of the British) Lloyds Bank,&quot; one dealer said after the evacuation at 1120 local time/1620 GMT, 10 minutes before trade usually begins.</p>
<p>((--Quito Newsroom, 5932 258429 x 113 e-mail: reuters1@reutersecu.com.ec))</p>
